{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790987704,"nonce":"/6cR5ZLpQdYoBUz8UQY/9Foo/So=","title":"Clip children of a transformed node exactly","message":"Since the transform commit, the display list clips the children of a transformed node with the overflow box's axis-aligned bounding box, without corner radii (blinc_abi/src/display_list.rs, append). A turned or slanted parent with overflow-hidden therefore lets children show past its rotated edges and its rounded corners (tools/snapshot/scenes/Transforms.hx, the last card). Exact: carry the clip as the clipping node's local rect plus its affine, and test the fragment's screen point in that frame (inverse 2x2) against the rounded rect, as Blinc's sdf_core does with clip_bounds in local space after its inverse transform.","files":null}]}